# Cursor AI Rules for Disaster Response Project

## Date and Time Generation
- Always use the MCP time server for generating current dates
- Use format: YYYY-MM-DD for all document filenames
- Current date context: Use MCP time server to get accurate timestamps
- For session notes, use format: YYYY-MM-DD-session-description.md
- For code improvement logs, use format: YYYY-MM-DD-improvement-description.md

## Project Structure
- Save trained models in @models/ directory
- Save experiment results in @results/ directory
- Use professional tone in all documentation
- Follow single responsibility principle for functions
- Keep functions under 50 lines when possible

## MCP Time Server Usage
- Query the time server for current date/time when generating filenames
- Use UTC timestamps for consistency
- Format dates as YYYY-MM-DD for file naming
